# Line endings for the Windows entry points.
#
# A .cmd file is read by cmd.exe, which expects CRLF; checking one out with LF endings is
# asking for trouble on a machine whose git is configured with core.autocrlf=false. The
# PowerShell scripts are pinned for the same reason — one file, one shape, on every clone.
#
# Everything else is left to git's own defaults so no existing file is renormalised.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
deploy/windows/*.ps1 text eol=crlf
